# Caddyfile for the hosted Xaya Roguelike sandbox.
#
# This box fronts the sandbox with a Cloudflare Tunnel (cloudflared): TLS is
# terminated at Cloudflare's edge and the tunnel forwards plain HTTP to Caddy
# on localhost:80. Caddy serves the static frontend and reverse-proxies game
# traffic to the local move proxy, which also relays read-only GSP calls
# (allowlisted, `stop` refused). anvil, xayax, and the GSP RPC stay bound to
# localhost; with the tunnel, no inbound port needs to be public at all.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Route the hostname to the tunnel:
#        cloudflared tunnel route dns <tunnel> <host>
#   2. Point the tunnel ingress at http://localhost:80 (see docs/DEPLOY.md).
#   3. Put the built frontend (index.html, style.css, dist/, assets/) at `root`.
#   4. caddy run --config devnet/deploy/Caddyfile   (or via systemd)
#
# To instead let Caddy terminate TLS directly (no tunnel), replace the `:80`
# site address below with your domain and open ports 80/443; Caddy then
# obtains and renews the certificate automatically.

:80 {
	encode gzip

	# Game traffic -> the move proxy (moves, GSP read relay, health check).
	@game path /gsp /proxy /proxy/*
	handle @game {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:18380
	}

	# Everything else -> the static frontend build.
	#
	# `current` is a symlink to the build being served (see deploy.sh).
	# Deploying is then a single atomic rename rather than a copy over live
	# files, so a browser loading the page mid-deploy can never get a
	# half-written bundle.
	handle {
		root * /var/www/rog-frontend/current
		try_files {path} /index.html
		file_server
	}
}
